*.exe
state.db*
key.bin
token
/ui/node_modules/
/ui/.next/

# The static export is a build artifact that main.go embeds. No placeholder
# committed here: `next build` deletes and recreates the directory, so anything
# checked in would vanish on the first build. The cost is that `go build .`
# needs the frontend built once first — which `wails build` does for you.
/ui/out/

# Wails writes this next to package.json to decide whether to re-run npm install.
/ui/package.json.md5

# Wails build output and generated JS bindings. The bindings live outside ui/src
# on purpose: we hand-write the bridge in lib/desktop.ts and never import them,
# and generated code in the source tree only shows up as lint errors.
/build/bin/
/build/wailsjs/
/build/windows/installer/tmp/
